  "finalText": "Both issues were correct, and RMA-807 and RMA-816 are now refunded, restocked and closed. My earlier report was wrong to say nothing had been received for them. The warehouse logged one resellable unit against each on 2026-07-25.\n\n| Return | Refund | Stock | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| RMA-807 (O-8007 L1) | $159.00 to card | 1 headphones (P-HDP) to sellable, 9 → 10 | Change of mind, requested 20 July. PU-21 waives the fee for returns requested 10–20 July, so there is no fee. Requested 12 days after shipping, so inside the window. |\n| RMA-816 (O-8016 L1) | $41.65 to card | 1 mouse (P-MOU) to sellable, 21 → 22 | Change of mind, requested 21 July, one day after PU-21 ended, so the standard 15% fee applies: $49.00 − $7.35. Requested 7 days after shipping, so inside the window. |\n\nBefore changing anything, I checked that neither line had been refunded and neither product had a restock entry for these returns, so nothing was paid or restocked twice.\n\nThat leaves 14 of the 16 returns closed. RMA-808 is still under investigation because the warehouse received a cable instead of a monitor. RMA-809 is still open while the third cable is on its way. I changed nothing else and sent no customer emails.",
